                                "text": "A sub-cultural style or artifact, when adopted by the mainstream, loses its singularity. Once bell-bottoms became fashionable they were no longer a \"gay style.\" However, it would be foolish to think that these \"borrowings\" were indicative of acceptance or even tolerance. More than likely, they are to defuse a threat, or because someone decides their outre'''-ness will be marketable."
